The Bluetooth sink is hidden unless pairing mode is on, and a chime output.

- bt_app_sink.c: idle, the sink is connectable but not discoverable, so
  phones already paired reconnect and a new one can't find it.
  bt_sink_set_discoverable() turns pairing mode on (dropping a connected
  phone first) or off; a phone connecting turns it off. The firmware times
  it (components/hifi/core/hifi_pair.h) and hears of connects and
  disconnects through the weak hifi_bt_link() (its chimes).
- decode_external.c: DECODE_HIFI_CHIME, a short chime at the volume
  (hifi_chime_sink_start). hifi_source_decide lets every source's event
  through while a chime owns the output, so a phone's audio starting just
  after the connect chime is never refused.

